  "claims": [
    "The preexisting explicit eleven-root legacy expansions and root-only contextual higher elimination are integrated into the current categorical/MAC presentation without adding coarse whole-context definition generators.",
    "The pure source categorical fragment has one new-rule rewrite per expanded old association/unit step; expansion agrees with the direct new encoding up to derived groupoid/context bookkeeping.",
    "For parallel source Composition tracks, actual legacy/current and legacy/legacy comparisons are generated using the preexisting finite source coherence and explicit root-definition bridges.",
    "The definition-use count equals actual legacy occurrences on the source categorical bridge; the legacy/legacy comparison has the sum of both source step counts.",
    "The combined-basis embeddings preserve every preexisting higher constructor count, and retain exact condition support.",
    "Arbitrary mixed-path boundary expansion preserves exact support, removes all old primitive labels, and has at most twenty new rewrite leaves per original rewrite leaf.",
    "Expansion fixes every label-clean track and is idempotent. Comparison witnesses can be transported in both directions between original and expanded boundaries with exactly the same support.",
    "Existence of comparisons is equivalent before and after boundary expansion within the same retained combined presentation.",
    "The existing three-family MAC normalization contract retargets to the combined basis; endpoint-only normalization after expansion retains the original path support.",
    "Repaired correlated past/state/input joint-law equality holds within the updated checked MAC model, including a supplied mixed placement."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The eleven-root expansion algorithm, root-only higher elimination, and finite source categorical coherence are reused from existing frozen files, not new general mathematics.",
    "Cross-encoding global coherence is restricted to images of parallel source Composition tracks. No full eighteen-rule or arbitrary tensor-internal coherence is supplied.",
    "Comparison equivalence retains the entire combined higher library. It is not elimination of old generators inside a higher witness, projection to a smaller basis, or proof of completeness.",
    "The twenty bound counts rewrite leaves, including formal proof inverses; it excludes context, wire and generator payload sizes and is not runtime or encoded certificate size.",
    "Definition calls and higher constructor counts are separate metrics. The existing four-context interchange fixture already has 2793 higher constructors for one definition use; no compression advantage is inferred.",
    "Endpoint-only normalization does not establish arbitrary root compatibility or the canonical tensor normalization square.",
    "The existing three normalization source families are unchanged; full structural/mixed finite coverage remains open.",
    "No new code-changing computational reduction, loss/time bound, complete native execution or key-generation integration, or fair total-cost advantage is proved.",
    "Unregistered NativeConfiguredMAC work remains outside the successful full-library build.",
    "Novelty remains unconfirmed. No new external primary-source reading or independent review was performed for this stage."
  ],
  "next_obligations": [
    "Construct the actual canonical tensor normalization comparison from finite justified local diagrams, then cover remaining Cartesian and mixed root interactions.",
    "Preserve full scope: finite schematic coverage, code-changing reductions and resource/loss contracts, continuing execution through oracle internals/keygen, fair shared-proof costs and theorem-level novelty assessment."
  ],
